risk: medium
confidence: medium
resolution: "SDK validators now own failed field, rejected value and enum-domain evidence; CLI guidance preserves producer attribution, canonical aliases, missing-ID operands and subcommand tokens without guessing from unrelated arguments. Review corrections add complete SDK get-depth metadata and grammar-aware registration without expanding ordinary option values."
expected_result: "Risk and deadline refusals identify their own validator surface and rejected value; missing-item failures identify lookup or ID; valid unrelated title and priority flags never determine attribution, and unknown attribution is omitted."
actual_result: "Final review correction proof for PR https://github.com/unbraind/pm-cli/pull/1376: 9638 tests passed, with exact source coverage 100/100/100/100 and zero uncovered counts: statements 66543/66543, branches 50900/50900, functions 13748/13748, lines 63446/63446. Strict static stages and type checking passed with no weakened policy; native linked commands passed with duplicate suppression. Packed manual Node/Bun acceptance passed 58 commands, preserving literal next tag values, canonical receipts, complete depth refusal evidence, rich full opt-in, and immutable history. All dependency severities and current GitHub security alert surfaces are zero; required Sentry/telemetry checks passed. First-head required CI passed and both actionable bot findings were implemented; the corrected-head hosted cycle remains required before merge. The prior v2026.10.3 publication predates this batch."
