learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-03T08:32:15.885Z","harness:codex","Agent context controls must either change the declared public result or fail before host preparation. Refusal ownership follows producer evidence, restore instructions execute under the original intent, and composition identities come from persisted mutation results. Tests must observe the public boundary and unchanged tracker state rather than mirror internal forwarding."
