body: "## Summary\nThe human detail identifies the invalid field, while machine-readable `refusal.surface` and `rejected_value` blame another valid input. This misdirects automated repair.\n\nReproduced with the official installed `@unbrained/pm-cli` 2026.9.30 on Linux, using disposable synthetic non-Git trackers. No implementation changes are included in this issue.\n\n## Reproduction\n```bash\nLAB=$(mktemp -d)\nmkdir -p \"$LAB/home\" \"$LAB/work\"\nexport HOME=\"$LAB/home\" PM_PATH=\"$LAB/work/.agents/pm\"\nexport PM_GLOBAL_PATH=\"$LAB/global\" PM_TELEMETRY_DISABLED=1\ncd \"$LAB/work\"\npm init \"$PM_PATH\" --defaults --author audit --agent-guidance skip --json >/dev/null\npm create task \"Audit sample\" --id t1 --description \"Execution detail\" --json >/dev/null\n```\n```bash\npm update pm-t1 --priority high --risk invalid --json\npm update pm-t1 --title x --risk invalid --json\npm update pm-t1 --title x --deadline not-a-date --json\npm update pm-missing --title x --json\n```\n\n## Actual\nFor the first command, exit 2:\n```json\n{\"code\":\"invalid_argument_value\",\"detail\":\"Invalid risk value \\\"invalid\\\". Allowed: low, medium, high, critical\",\"refusal\":{\"surface\":\"--priority\",\"rejected_value\":\"high\",\"exit_code\":2}}\n```\nWith title preceding invalid risk or deadline, the refusal instead names `--title` / `x`. A missing-item update also attributes the refusal to a valid title flag. Structured consumers therefore receive different, false repair targets depending on unrelated arguments.\n\n## Expected\nRisk validation names `--risk` and `invalid`; deadline validation names `--deadline` and `not-a-date`; a missing item names the ID/lookup surface. If precise attribution is unavailable, omit it rather than inventing an offending flag.\n\n## Implementation plan\n1. Carry validator-owned structured metadata (surface, rejected value, legal domain where available) with the typed error from its origin.\n2. Have the shared refusal renderer preserve that metadata. Remove fallback attribution based on the first/last supplied flag or argument order.\n3. Give lookup and policy errors their own meaningful surfaces, independent of mutation options.\n4. Keep detail, recovery and refusal metadata consistent across CLI/SDK adapters; document nullable/absent attribution.\n5. Add parameterized conformance tests over validators and argument permutations.\n\n## Regression acceptance\n- [ ] Risk, deadline and missing-ID fixtures identify the actual failure\n- [ ] Permuting valid title/priority flags never changes attribution\n- [ ] Attached values, aliases, multiple invalid inputs and no flagged inputs are covered\n- [ ] Error paths do not mutate item state\n- [ ] Unknown attribution is omitted; legal-domain values correspond to the blamed field\n- [ ] Existing policy-specific missing-field and surface tests remain green\n\n## Ownership and duplicate check\nChild of #1363; use as a structured-refusal negative control in #1362. Related closed #1305 fixed require_fields policy metadata. These current ordinary value-validation and missing-item cases require no workflow policy and are not covered by that narrow report. Open and closed issues were searched for refusal and rejected_value."
